<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martos is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaen">Jaén</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, below the rock known as the Peña de Martos; it was the Roman colony of Tucci. Its castle was handed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a> by al-Bayyasi in the 1220s and then given to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-calatrava">Order of Calatrava</a>, which held it as a frontier stronghold facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>. The town is now a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a> production.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martos.jpg" alt="Martos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xapis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pe%C3%B1a_de_Martos.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
